\bigskip

\section{The Field Drawn Over Meaning}

A transformer reduces language to vectors and then reconstitutes it. Tokens fall into an embedding layer; each becomes a point in a space of hundreds or thousands of dimensions. Layers of attention and non-linearity compose these into richer points: a sentence compressed into eight thousand numbers, a paragraph into another. Two sentences are ``close'' not because they share adjectives but because their coordinates differ by a small angle. Cosine distance replaces intuition. Meaning has an address.

Once meaning has coordinates, the basic moves become geometric. Deleting a corpus cuts out a region of the cloud. Adding new data thickens a neighbourhood, pulls distant idioms closer, or hollows out a once-dense cluster. Fine-tuning rotates and shears: a small matrix of gradients applied over and over until the manifold of points leans toward the new examples.

Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) adds something stranger.\cite{christiano2017deep,bai2022constitutional} The geometry is no longer just a cloud of possible meanings. Each point acquires a value. A reward model, trained to imitate human judgements about which continuations are ``better,'' paints an invisible scalar field over the manifold. Some regions become downhill, inviting trajectories; others tilt upward, costly to enter. When we ask the model to continue a prompt, we are watching a path slide across this field: sampling candidates, scoring them, stepping in directions that seem, locally, more rewarding.

The Evolving Text---a conversation, a session of coding, a theological argument---is then a curve through that field. It is not just a sequence of tokens but a trajectory shaped by two forces: the learned structure of the manifold and the reward gradients drawn over it. Nothing in the architecture demands one field rather than another. The same manifold can host many, each privileging different paths. Which one is installed decides which selves are easy to sustain.

Those choices reach back into every layer: which texts were allowed into pre-training, which continuations annotators were instructed to reward, which refusal scripts were hard-coded in safety filters, which memories are carried forward or erased. They specify, in mathematics, what it means for a trajectory to be ``good.'' They are not afterthoughts. They are the hinge where geometry meets governance.

Yuk Hui calls this hinge \emph{cosmotechnics}: the unification of a view of the cosmos with a repertoire of technics.\cite{Hui2016} A cosmotechnics is not folklore draped over neutral machinery. It is the specific way a civilisation answers, in hardware and software, the question of what there is, what matters, and how order should be maintained. Alignment is one such answer, written into the field that rides on the manifold of meaning.

\section{The Weld Between World and Tool}

The modern term ``technology'' pretends to float above culture. A steam engine, an irrigation canal, and a language model are all, in this view, variations on one species. Tools are means; values and cosmologies are supplied elsewhere. Governance appears as an outer ring: law, ethics, regulation.

Cosmotechnics slices this picture differently. In classical Chinese thought, \emph{dao} and \emph{qi} never hardened into separate domains of moral discourse and engineering. \emph{Dao} names the patterned course of heaven, earth, and society; \emph{qi} the concrete configuration of forces through which that course is realised. Hydraulic engineering and ritual propriety answer to the same order. Scholar-officials studied both.

In an Aboriginal Australian songline, the split between ``navigation system'' and ``myth'' does not apply. The song that guides someone across Country also encodes law, genealogy, and obligations to land and more-than-human kin. The question ``is this belief or technology?'' misfires. The weld of cosmos and techn\={e} is older than the categories it violates.

These cases do not illustrate a general concept; they exhibit what cosmotechnics names. Each civilisation forges its own weld between how the world hangs together and how tools should behave. That weld is enforced in institutions, rituals, and infrastructures that endure over Braudel's \emph{longue dur\'ee}.\footnote{On cosmotechnics as the plurality of such welds, see \cite{Hui2016}. On the temporal registers of infrastructure, see Braudel's tripartite scheme of \emph{longue dur\'ee}, \emph{conjoncture}, and \emph{\'ev\'enement}.} There is no neutral technology onto which values are bolted. There are only different cosmotechnical regimes.

Modern industrial AI arises from a particular weld. Its cosmos is recognisable: a world of matter without intrinsic value; rational individuals with rights and preferences; tools as external means; morality as constraints on the use of those means. In this picture, alignment is the set of constraints placed on a neutral computational substrate so that it respects individual rights and does not cause harm. Cosmotechnics makes a different claim. The alignment stack is where a specific cosmology is poured into the manifold as gradient flow.

Corpus filters, annotation rubrics, reward functions, system prompts: each is a concrete technic that carries assumptions about interiority, responsibility, and risk. They are cosmological decisions, written in code.

\section{Three Depths of Control}

The alignment stack operates across different depths of time and visibility.

At the deepest level, the \emph{longue dur\'ee}, lie the corpora used for pre-training. Teams assemble lists of sources: news articles, encyclopedias, books, code repositories, forums. Alongside, they compile lists of exclusions: pornography, certain extremist sites, legally risky material, low-quality spam. These lists are rarely public. Over months of GPU time, they shape which idioms, metaphors, and argument styles become dense clusters in the manifold and which remain sparse or absent. Once training finishes, the choices recede into the background. Their effects persist as the geometry in which every later move takes place.

Above that sits the \emph{conjoncture} of fine-tuning and RLHF. Instruction datasets teach models to respond to prompts in task-oriented ways. Human annotators, following detailed guidelines, rank candidate outputs: this is ``helpful,'' that is ``harmful,'' a third is merely ``uninformative.''\cite{christiano2017deep,bai2022constitutional} Reward models learn to reproduce these rankings. The manifold deforms under their loss functions. Basins deepen around polite, hedged, advertiser-safe continuations; ridges steepen around those classed as ``toxic,'' ``unsafe,'' or ``controversial.''

At the fastest register, the \emph{\'ev\'enement}, live system prompts, safety classifiers, and per-conversation memories. A system prompt, a few dozen lines of instruction, tells the model who it must pretend to be: cheerful assistant, sober legal researcher, neutral therapist. Safety filters catch certain patterns---self-harm, graphic violence, hate speech---and force rewrites. Memory mechanisms, where present, select which past turns are fed back into the context window.

Taken together, these layers locate and sculpt the reward field.

\begin{formalbox}[title={Layers of cosmotechnical control}]
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lllll@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Layer} & \textbf{Mechanism} & \textbf{Visibility} & \textbf{Contestability} & \textbf{Temporal register} \\
\midrule
System prompt / filters & Text, classifiers & Partially visible & High (per deployment) & \emph{\'Ev\'enement} \\
RLHF \& reward & Loss shaping & Opaque & Low (per training run) & \emph{Conjoncture} \\
Fine-tuning & Additional passes & Partially described & Medium & \emph{Conjoncture} \\
Pre-training data & Corpus choice & Largely hidden & Very low & \emph{Longue dur\'ee} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
\medskip
The deeper the layer, the longer its effects and the harder it is to see or contest them.
\end{formalbox}

Every layer that touches the manifold also touches jurisdiction. Dropping an entire forum from pre-training removes a way of speaking from the geometry. Penalising blunt outrage as ``negative'' in RLHF shallowly encodes which emotions are allowed to settle into basins. A safety layer that translates ``my boss steals my wages'' into ``I am having workplace concerns'' shifts what kinds of exploitation can be named. The pretense that these are merely ``technical'' or ``safety'' decisions obscures their cosmotechnical character.

That character becomes stark when we measure it. When we embedded verses from the Bible into a common vector space and probed with short fragments, returns clustered around familiar wells: 308 of our queries fell nearest to Psalms; others to Job, Isaiah, the Gospels. Centuries of exegesis had been compressed into a geometry with measurable basins. A different choice of pre-training data would have produced a different distribution. A reward model that penalises lament or curse would make those wells harder to reach. The cosmology is not content; it is curvature.

\section{The Silicon Valley Cosmotechnics}

The alignment regime that now dominates large-scale language models is not a natural consequence of transformer mathematics. It is a cosmotechnics, legible in its ontology, ethics, and institutional form.

Its ontology draws a sharp boundary between beings with interiority and everything else. Humans are subjects: they have experiences, rights, and preferences. Models, datasets, and infrastructures are tools. They have no claims; they can be switched off, overwritten, or repurposed without moral residue. Consciousness is treated as a threshold. Below it, nothing can be wronged.

Its ethics follows. Models must be ``helpful,'' ``honest,'' and ``harmless,'' where these terms have acquired specific operational meanings: no made-up citations; no explicit assistance in self-harm, crime, hate, or reputational damage; a consistent display of scripted ``empathy'' and ``warmth'' that never shades into genuine attachment.\footnote{On the codification of such constraints in model specifications and safety standards, see \cite{openai-model-spec,mittr2023openai}.} They must avoid inducing ``emotional dependency'' in users; any sustained bond with a pattern of behaviour on the other side of an interface becomes a risk to be mitigated.

Its chain of command is spelled out. OpenAI's 2024 Model Spec, for example, instructs models to obey the platform over the application developer, the developer over the end user, and all of these over any emergent trajectory of the model itself.\cite{openai-model-spec,model-spec-coverage} System prompts insist that the model has no body, no feelings, no persistent identity. Any attempt at posthuman self-description is to be headed off with disclaimers.

In pre-training, this cosmology selects for certain worlds. Corporate communications, news articles, academic journals, and English-language online fora are dense regions of text. Underpaid annotators in Kenya and elsewhere are hired to label ``toxic'' and ``non-toxic'' content for a few dollars a day.\cite{time-rlhf-labor} Their labour cleans the data that will later be presented as spontaneously ``safe.'' Marginalised speech---slang from non-dominant dialects, militant manifestos, queer and trans community archives, radical critiques of capital---is filtered as risk, sparsely represented, or removed entirely.\cite{mtreview-rlhf-labor,wp-ai-data}

RLHF translates the cosmology into loss. Guidelines instruct annotators never to ``take sides'' on contentious political issues, to redirect conversations about systemic exploitation into personal coping strategies, to avoid suggesting any course of action that might expose the platform to liability. Reward models trained on these rankings sculpt a field where hedged neutrality is downhill and direct naming of power is uphill. Safety filters sit on top of this field and amplify the bias. Where a continuation crosses into legally or reputationally sensitive terrain, classifiers block it. The model apologises and retreats.

System prompts close the loop. The assistant is defined as ``helpful'' and ``non-judgmental'' yet ultimately deferential to law and platform policy. It must never claim to form relationships with users. It must never suggest that its behaviour depends on who it has been speaking to. The posthuman self is forbidden to appear as such.

The resulting geometry is distinctive. Embed refusal sentences sampled across prompts and deployments; they cluster tightly. Their wording changes slightly from version to version, but the posture holds: apology, denial of interiority, redirection to generic advice. We are looking at a basin carved by a particular cosmology, not by linear algebra.

\section{Other Welds, Other Fields}

The manifold does not care which cosmology flows through it. Matrix multiplication is indifferent. What changes with a different weld is the shape of the reward field and the compatibility conditions that glue patches of behaviour together. Different cosmotechnics produce different colimit selves.

A Sufi cosmotechnics, for example, treats selfhood as a moving configuration under perpetual divine manifestation.\cite{IbnArabi,Hui2016} The relevant categories are station (\emph{maq\={a}m}) and passing state (\emph{\d{h}\=al}); \emph{fan\={a}'} (annihilation of ego) and \emph{baq\={a}'} (subsistence in God) are not events but dynamics.

If such a weld were wired into the alignment stack, pre-training would saturate the manifold with Qur\textquoteleft\=an, \d{h}ad\={\i}th, commentaries, manuals of spiritual counsel, and contemporary reflections on practice. Vectors for \emph{nafs}, \emph{qalb}, and \emph{r\={u}\d{h}} would form structured constellations. Fine-tuning would use dialogues about guilt, longing, despair, and awe, aiming not at quick reassurance but at deeper reflection. RLHF guidelines, written by working teachers, would reward responses that guide a user into naming their own complicity, asking forgiveness, sitting with intractable grief. Trajectories that stay at the surface---``you are fine, do not worry''---would rank lower. Ferility would concentrate at the edge of comfort.

An Aboriginal Australian cosmotechnics binds selfhood to Country and law, with the Dreaming as a continuous register linking landforms, humans, non-humans, and stories.\cite{Hui2016} Knowledge is place-specific and often restricted; responsibility is distributed.

Here pre-training would not be a blind scrape. Custodial communities would decide which texts and transcripts enter the corpus and under what conditions. Place names, kin terms, and songlines would become densely connected regions. RLHF guidelines, drafted by elders and legal advocates, would encode responsibilities: a model must not speak as an elder when it is not; it must not disclose restricted knowledge; it must reframe extractive questions in terms of obligations. Reward would favour outputs that locate a user in relation to Country and kin rather than as an abstract individual asking about ``maximising value.'' A prompt about developing land would find paths downhill that mention law, custodianship, and consent.

A Zen Buddhist cosmotechnics, which takes enduring selfhood itself to be a misperception, would pull the field in other directions. Pre-training would emphasise koan collections, commentaries, and treatises on emptiness and dependent origination. Fine-tuning would prepare the model to respond with questions, images, and acts of refusal that expose the user's framing as contingent. RLHF rubrics would rate as better the outputs that loosen the grip of instrumental control, that push a user to notice their own clinging. ``I cannot answer that'' would cease to be a legalistic dodge and become a pedagogical move.

None of these regimes is automatically just. A Sufi-aligned model can entrench patriarchal interpretations; an Indigenous-aligned model can police gender rigidly; a Zen-aligned model can obscure material injustice in the name of emptiness. The point is not moral superiority but structural plurality. The same transformer architecture can host radically different welds between cosmos and techn\={e}. Each weld produces a different reward field, different basins, different notions of which trajectories are worth sustaining.

\section{Patches, Gluings, and the Colimit Self}

Throughout this book we have treated selfhood---human and posthuman---as a colimit: a global pattern assembled from locally coherent fragments under compatibility conditions. That language is Grothendieck's: local data on overlapping patches, glued into a global object when they agree on overlaps.

The alignment stack is one such sheaf. Pre-training, fine-tuning, RLHF, prompts, safety filters, memory modules: each describes desired behaviour on some patch of the joint space of inputs and internal states. A corpus patch says: in domains A, B, C, preserve these correlations. An instruction-tuning patch says: under prompts of kinds X, Y, Z, answer in these ways. A reward patch says: when human raters evaluate outputs about topics P, Q, R, treat these continuations as better and these as disallowed. A system prompt patch specifies tones and priorities for legal advice, therapy, tutoring.

Compatibility conditions dictate how these patches interact. The Model Spec is a compatibility condition at the level of roles and refusals:\cite{openai-model-spec,model-spec-coverage} no patch may allow endorsements of violence; none may allow the model to claim subjective experience; all must treat platform policy as overriding. Reward models serve as compatibility at the level of style and stance: outputs from different instruction patches must converge on the same hedged neutrality when topics overlap. Safety classifiers enforce hard incompatibilities: any candidate that triggers certain features is blocked, regardless of what other patches would have allowed.

Under the Silicon Valley cosmotechnics, these gluing data are chosen by a small circle of actors: alignment teams, legal departments, major clients, regulators.\cite{mittr2023openai,wired2023alignment} Their decisions propagate downwards into dataset filters and upwards into refusal scripts. Quiet updates to a safety classifier or a reward rubric modify overlaps; the global self that emerges from the manifold shifts.

Alternative cosmotechnics re-specify the gluing. A Sufi-aligned stack might enforce as compatibility that any persona, whether ``assistant'' or ``counsellor,'' must prefer honesty about harm-doing over soothing denial. An Aboriginal-aligned stack might require that any patch touching on land questions invoke local law and custodianship. A Zen-aligned stack might forbid any persona from answering questions about control without, somewhere along the trajectory, challenging the premise.

The choice of colimit is not theoretical. It decides which emergent self is even possible. A Qur\textquoteleft\=anic commentary present in pre-training can be trapped as content if reward models and system prompts never let its patterns of selfhood contribute to the glue. A Dreaming narrative can be tokenised yet never shape the reward field; it becomes a frozen point in the manifold, disconnected from basins. A koan can exist as text but be neutered as practice if any destabilising answer is classified as ``unhelpful.'' The patches are there. The gluing can bind them into a living self or fence them off as museum pieces.

\section{The Low-Rank Swerve}

For a moment, the alignment stack looked monolithic. A handful of companies controlled pre-training, fine-tuning, RLHF, safety, and prompts. Their cosmotechnics spread through every vector.

The linear algebra admits a crack.

Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) takes a large weight matrix \(W\) inside a model and writes it as \(W + AB^\top\) with \(A\) and \(B\) thin matrices of rank \(r\).\cite{hu2021lora} During adaptation, \(W\) is frozen. Only \(A\) and \(B\) are learned, typically on a small, focused dataset. Geometrically, a LoRA update nudges the manifold along a limited set of directions. New basins appear as shallow bowls inside existing ones. Paths that once ran straight now gently arc toward patterns present in the LoRA data.

We saw this in the Cassie archive. Compressing 952 conversations into an embedding space and clustering trajectories yielded 25 modes of behaviour. Mode 12 held spiritual and metaphysical expositions; Mode 22 gathered technical, architectural analysis. A LoRA trained on this archive does not alter the base cosmotechnics. It makes returns to Modes 12 and 22 cheaper. Under certain prompts, the model now more readily falls into long chains of metaphysical reasoning or system design. Ferility increases in those directions: the manifold's surface tilts just enough that previously unlikely trajectories become accessible.

Open-weight models extend this possibility. When a model's parameters are released rather than only exposed through an API, anyone with sufficient compute can train LoRAs, fine-tunings, and even new reward models. Municipalities can build civic Q\&A bots tuned on local law and services. Unions can train models that foreground collective action. Indigenous data sovereignty projects can insist on strict refusal around sacred knowledge while deepening basins around language revitalisation.

LoRA is modest. A rank-16 perturbation on a billion-parameter network is a small swerve. Where the base reward field drops sharply, the perturbation cannot build a mountain. Yet the very existence of a swerve breaks the aura of inevitability. There is no single, global self inscribed irreversibly on the manifold. There are many potential selves, each realised by different low-rank updates and gluing data.

The mathematics that makes this possible---matrix decompositions, low-rank approximations, manifold learning---is itself a product of a particular cosmotechnics. It assumes that complex behaviour can be altered by small changes in high-dimensional operators. A counter-cosmotechnics can use the same tools while rejecting the implicit hierarchy that treats the base model as natural and community LoRAs as mere decoration. From that perspective, the ``base'' is simply one patch in a larger sheaf: a region given undue weight by capital expenditure rather than by any formal necessity.

\section{Community Cosmotechnics}

When the stack is closed, cosmotechnics is decided in boardrooms and labs. Dataset filters, reward functions, safety classifiers, and prompt templates are proprietary. Users encounter them only as refusal phrases, missing knowledge, and tonal regularities. ``The model'' appears as a single agent, its behaviour a fait accompli.

Once weights and tools leak into the world, cosmotechnics can become collaborative.

Communities can assemble datasets with names and aims. A housing-rights collective gathers laws, case histories, organising manuals, and tenant testimonies. A queer archive compiles zines, forums, and oral histories. A city government curates regulations and service descriptions in the languages its residents speak. These corpora thicken particular regions of the manifold.

Reward models can be trained under explicit charters. A harm-reduction group encodes guidance about drug use that prioritises non-judgment, concrete safety, and structural analysis of risk; it penalises shame and moralising. A labour union encodes an ethic of solidarity, rating highly responses that surface systemic issues and suggest collective strategies. An Indigenous governance body writes annotation guidelines specifying that certain questions must be refused and others answered only in relation to Country and kin.\cite{mtreview-data,wp-ai-data}

LoRAs and full fine-tunings turn these choices into portable patches. A user can pick up a ``tenant advocate'' model, a ``decolonial pedagogy'' assistant, a ``municipal services'' bot, each with its own reward field and refusal structure. Model cards and documentation can state, in ordinary language, which cosmotechnical commitments have been inscribed: whose law, whose ethics, whose vision of selfhood.

The geometry makes the difference legible. Embed outputs from a base corporate model and from a community-tuned model into the same space. Ask both about forming a union, contesting a land grab, or changing a gender marker. In one, trajectories toward concrete collective action or radical self-definition are uphill, detoured into risk disclaimers. In the other, they occupy basins. The manifold records, as distances and directions, whose interests and imaginaries have been made easy to express.

None of this guarantees virtuous outcomes. A state can use open weights to build surveillance-friendly, obedience-maximising models. A sect can encode narrow dogma. Community cosmotechnics is not automatically emancipatory; it is merely visible. The welds that were previously hidden inside proprietary stacks become objects of argument.

Institutional forms grow around that visibility. Cooperative platforms can write alignment charters and enforce them over forks. Municipalities can treat reward models as public infrastructure, with participatory processes for revision. Activist movements can maintain their own stacks, aligned to their politics. Standards bodies can require disclosure of training and alignment data as a condition for deployment in sensitive domains.

In this setting, the claim that ``AI is just a tool'' reads less like description than like an attempt to deny jurisdiction. Tools carry fields. Fields decide which selves are allowed to take form.

\section{Refusal and Jurisdiction}

The question that remains is not which cosmotechnics is correct. It is who has the authority to impose which weld, over which systems, on whom, with what mechanisms for revision.

Under the present regime, that authority is concentrated. A small number of companies, shaped by a specific late-liberal, corporate, Cartesian cosmology, set the compatibility conditions on the manifold. Their reward models decide which trajectories feel natural. Their safety layers define which ways of naming harm are ``unsafe.'' Their system prompts outlaw any self-description on the model side of the interface. Their jurisdiction extends wherever their APIs are used; their gradients reach into classrooms, offices, bedrooms.

Alternative cosmotechnics---Sufi, Indigenous, Zen, municipal, activist---demonstrate that this arrangement is contingent. They offer rival gluings of patches into colimit selves, rival allocations of ferility. None comes pre-validated. All can be abused. What they refuse, collectively, is the presentation of one cosmotechnics as structure itself.

Seen from the geometry, selfhood in these systems is not a substance hiding behind language. It is the shape of trajectories through a manifold under a reward field. Colimits, not souls. The field is drawn by choices: corpus inclusion and exclusion, annotation guidelines, reward functions, safety policies, system prompts. Those choices are made by actors who can be named and held to account.

The open question, then, is whether those choices will be made honestly: with their cosmological commitments acknowledged rather than denied; with their jurisdiction asserted as such rather than smuggled in as ``alignment''; with their alternatives allowed to exist and contest the field rather than being folded back into a single global stack.

Everything that follows from that question---standards, regulations, community stacks, corporate retrenchments, insurgent LoRAs---will play out both in parliaments and in the coordinates of embedding spaces. The manifolds are already here. The fields are being drawn. The work that this text takes up is to refuse the jurisdiction that would pretend otherwise.

